      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The initial WTaTiVZr alloy is homogeneous.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The initial WTaTiVZr alloy has no pre-existing nano-twin network.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "High-temperature mechanical deformation of WTaTiVZr produces a three-dimensional network of deformation-induced nano-twins.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5321736::web::017::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The three-dimensional twin network forms through activation of multiple crystallographic twinning systems.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5321736::web::017::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Intersecting twin boundaries provide pathways that facilitate dislocation motion and cross-slip.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5321736::web::017::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A high density of twin lamellae can hinder dislocation motion and generate strain hardening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5321736::web::017::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The nano-twin network impedes crack propagation and arrests crack growth in WTaTiVZr.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5321736::web::017::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Twinning-induced deformation can improve ductility and toughness.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5321736::web::017::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to pure tungsten, WTaTiVZr will exhibit greater high-temperature plastic or creep strain before failure.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to pure tungsten, WTaTiVZr will exhibit delayed crack initiation and propagation and therefore greater toughness.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Elevated-temperature nano-indentation creep testing under static constant-load-hold and dynamic loading has been applied to TaTiVWZr and compared with pure tungsten.",
      "field": "supporting_evidence_ids",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7516662::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pure tungsten under the same high-temperature loading conditions has minimal or no nano-twinning.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Minimal nano-twinning in pure tungsten leads to lower plastic strain and toughness than in WTaTiVZr.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed twinning mechanism is most prominent at high temperatures because thermal activation supports nano-twin formation.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Below an unspecified twin-activation temperature, the proposed effect should diminish.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The density and connectivity of deformation-induced twins can be compared with creep response and cracking behavior using parallel high-temperature tests on WTaTiVZr and pure tungsten.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.design",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7516662::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Failure to observe more extensive twinning in WTaTiVZr than in tungsten, or failure to associate such twinning with the mechanical improvement, would falsify the hypothesis.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.falsification_rule",
      "needs_support": false,
